§ `Tests -- Form 5.041, quoting section 487.0551(1): a warrant for arrest in Form 5.062`

-- "If a person fails to appear at the place, day and time set out in an order made under subsection 487.051(4) or 487.055(3.11) or in a summons referred to in subsection 487.055(4) or 487.091(3)"
#ASSERT `form 5.041 as quoted from section 487.0551(1) a justice of the peace may issue a warrant for the arrest in Form 5.062` TRUE `forms 5.041 and 5.061 an order made under subsection 487.051(4)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `form 5.041 as quoted from section 487.0551(1) a justice of the peace may issue a warrant for the arrest in Form 5.062` TRUE `forms 5.041 and 5.061 an order made under subsection 487.055(3.11)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `form 5.041 as quoted from section 487.0551(1) a justice of the peace may issue a warrant for the arrest in Form 5.062` TRUE `forms 5.041 and 5.061 a summons referred to in subsection 487.055(4)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `form 5.041 as quoted from section 487.0551(1) a justice of the peace may issue a warrant for the arrest in Form 5.062` TRUE `forms 5.041 and 5.061 a summons referred to in subsection 487.091(3)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- the "If" is unmet: the person appeared
-- RECONCILED 2026-11-12: was `#ASSERT `form 5.041 as quoted from section 487.0551(1) a justice of the peace may issue a warrant for the arrest in Form 5.062` FALSE `forms 5.041 and 5.061 an order made under subsection 487.051(4)` EQUALS JUST FALSE`; the name is a "may" that gives a power or liberty and its "If" gate is unmet; the text limits the grant in its own wording and is silent outside the limit, so the answer is NOTHING, not a "may not" (name-test sweep, fork F-W; the other reading, a failed "If" as the text's own no, is JUST FALSE).
#ASSERT `form 5.041 as quoted from section 487.0551(1) a justice of the peace may issue a warrant for the arrest in Form 5.062` FALSE `forms 5.041 and 5.061 an order made under subsection 487.051(4)` EQUALS NOTHING
-- an instrument the sentence does not list: not covered
#ASSERT `form 5.041 as quoted from section 487.0551(1) a justice of the peace may issue a warrant for the arrest in Form 5.062` TRUE `forms 5.041 and 5.061 an order made under subsection 196.14(4) or 196.24(4) of the National Defence Act` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `form 5.041 as quoted from section 487.0551(1) a justice of the peace may issue a warrant for the arrest in Form 5.062` TRUE `forms 5.041 and 5.061 another instrument` EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Tests -- Form 5.041, quoting section 487.0552(1): the offence, its class and its punishment`

-- "Every person who, without reasonable excuse, fails to comply with an order made under subsection 487.051(4) or 487.055(3.11) ... or under subsection 196.14(4) or 196.24(4) of the National Defence Act, or with a summons referred to in subsection 487.055(4) or 487.091(3) ..., is guilty of"
#ASSERT `form 5.041 as quoted from section 487.0552(1) the person is guilty of an offence` TRUE FALSE `forms 5.041 and 5.061 an order made under subsection 487.051(4)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `form 5.041 as quoted from section 487.0552(1) the person is guilty of an offence` TRUE FALSE `forms 5.041 and 5.061 an order made under subsection 487.055(3.11)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `form 5.041 as quoted from section 487.0552(1) the person is guilty of an offence` TRUE FALSE `forms 5.041 and 5.061 an order made under subsection 196.14(4) or 196.24(4) of the National Defence Act` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `form 5.041 as quoted from section 487.0552(1) the person is guilty of an offence` TRUE FALSE `forms 5.041 and 5.061 a summons referred to in subsection 487.055(4)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `form 5.041 as quoted from section 487.0552(1) the person is guilty of an offence` TRUE FALSE `forms 5.041 and 5.061 a summons referred to in subsection 487.091(3)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- a reasonable excuse, a person who did not fail to comply, and an instrument not listed: not covered
#ASSERT `form 5.041 as quoted from section 487.0552(1) the person is guilty of an offence` TRUE TRUE `forms 5.041 and 5.061 an order made under subsection 487.051(4)` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `form 5.041 as quoted from section 487.0552(1) the person is guilty of an offence` FALSE FALSE `forms 5.041 and 5.061 an order made under subsection 487.051(4)` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `form 5.041 as quoted from section 487.0552(1) the person is guilty of an offence` TRUE FALSE `forms 5.041 and 5.061 another instrument` EQUALS NOTHING

-- the class: two limbs, indictable (a) or summary (b)
#ASSERT `form 5.041 as quoted from section 487.0552(1) the class of offence` EQUALS `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`
-- limb (a): "liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than two years"; no minimum and no fine is stated
#ASSERT `form 5.041 as quoted from section 487.0552(1)(a) the punishment on indictment` EQUALS Punishment WITH `mode` IS `by indictment`, `maximum imprisonment` IS `imprisonment for a term of` (`Length of time` OF 2, 0, 0, FALSE), `minimum imprisonment` IS `no imprisonment is stated`, `maximum fine` IS `no fine is stated`, `minimum fine` IS `no fine is stated`
-- limb (b): "an offence punishable on summary conviction": this text states no punishment for it
#ASSERT `form 5.041 as quoted from section 487.0552(1)(b) the punishment on summary conviction` EQUALS Punishment WITH `mode` IS `on summary conviction`, `maximum imprisonment` IS `no imprisonment is stated`, `minimum imprisonment` IS `no imprisonment is stated`, `maximum fine` IS `no fine is stated`, `minimum fine` IS `no fine is stated`

§ `Tests -- Form 5.041, the warnings and the order to appear`

#ASSERT `form 5.041 warning: failure to appear in accordance with the order may result in a warrant being issued for the arrest` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `form 5.041 warning: failure to appear in accordance with the order may result in a warrant being issued for the arrest` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `form 5.041 warning: failure to appear, without reasonable excuse, is an offence under subsection 487.0552(1)` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `form 5.041 warning: failure to appear, without reasonable excuse, is an offence under subsection 487.0552(1)` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `form 5.041 warning: failure to appear, without reasonable excuse, is an offence under subsection 487.0552(1)` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- "order you ... to appear on (date)": with 14 days until the day set out, appearing at day 10 or at day 14 -> FULFILLED; not appearing by day 15 -> BREACH.
#TRACE `form 5.041 the person must appear for the taking of bodily substances` 14 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `forms 1 to 23 the person to whom the demand, order or summons is addressed` DOES `forms 5.041 and 5.061 appears at the place, day and time set out for the taking of bodily substances` AT 10

#TRACE `form 5.041 the person must appear for the taking of bodily substances` 14 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `forms 1 to 23 the person to whom the demand, order or summons is addressed` DOES `forms 5.041 and 5.061 appears at the place, day and time set out for the taking of bodily substances` AT 14

#TRACE `form 5.041 the person must appear for the taking of bodily substances` 14 AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 15

§ `Tests -- Form 5.061, the second quotation of the same two sections, the warnings, the command and the force`

#ASSERT `form 5.061 as quoted from section 487.0551(1) a justice of the peace may issue a warrant for the arrest in Form 5.062` TRUE `forms 5.041 and 5.061 a summons referred to in subsection 487.055(4)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- RECONCILED 2026-11-12: was `#ASSERT `form 5.061 as quoted from section 487.0551(1) a justice of the peace may issue a warrant for the arrest in Form 5.062` FALSE `forms 5.041 and 5.061 a summons referred to in subsection 487.055(4)` EQUALS JUST FALSE`; the name is a "may" that gives a power or liberty and its "If" gate is unmet; the text limits the grant in its own wording and is silent outside the limit, so the answer is NOTHING, not a "may not" (name-test sweep, fork F-W; the other reading, a failed "If" as the text's own no, is JUST FALSE).
#ASSERT `form 5.061 as quoted from section 487.0551(1) a justice of the peace may issue a warrant for the arrest in Form 5.062` FALSE `forms 5.041 and 5.061 a summons referred to in subsection 487.055(4)` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `form 5.061 as quoted from section 487.0551(1) a justice of the peace may issue a warrant for the arrest in Form 5.062` TRUE `forms 5.041 and 5.061 another instrument` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `form 5.061 as quoted from section 487.0552(1) the person is guilty of an offence` TRUE FALSE `forms 5.041 and 5.061 a summons referred to in subsection 487.091(3)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `form 5.061 as quoted from section 487.0552(1) the person is guilty of an offence` TRUE TRUE `forms 5.041 and 5.061 a summons referred to in subsection 487.091(3)` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `form 5.061 as quoted from section 487.0552(1) the class of offence` EQUALS `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`
#ASSERT `form 5.061 as quoted from section 487.0552(1)(a) the punishment on indictment`'s `maximum imprisonment` EQUALS `imprisonment for a term of` (`Length of time` OF 2, 0, 0, FALSE)
#ASSERT `form 5.061 as quoted from section 487.0552(1)(b) the punishment on summary conviction`'s `mode` EQUALS `on summary conviction`
#ASSERT `form 5.061 warning: failure to appear in accordance with the summons may result in a warrant being issued for the arrest` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `form 5.061 warning: failure to appear in accordance with the summons may result in a warrant being issued for the arrest` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `form 5.061 warning: failure to appear, without reasonable excuse, is an offence under subsection 487.0552(1)` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `form 5.061 warning: failure to appear, without reasonable excuse, is an offence under subsection 487.0552(1)` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

-- "to command you ... to appear": 7 days until the day set out; appearing at day 7 -> FULFILLED; not appearing by day 8 -> BREACH.
#TRACE `form 5.061 the person must appear for the taking of bodily substances` 7 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `forms 1 to 23 the person to whom the demand, order or summons is addressed` DOES `forms 5.041 and 5.061 appears at the place, day and time set out for the taking of bodily substances` AT 7

#TRACE `form 5.061 the person must appear for the taking of bodily substances` 7 AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 8

-- "A peace officer, or a person who is acting under a peace officer's direction, who takes the samples ... may use as much force as necessary to do so."
#ASSERT `form 5.061 the person may use the force used` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- a person outside the two named; a person not taking the samples; more force than necessary: each outside the grant's words, so not covered (not "may not")
#ASSERT `form 5.061 the person may use the force used` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `form 5.061 the person may use the force used` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `form 5.061 the person may use the force used` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

